# serialize_plan_mode() wire-format digests: sha256 + byte length per query.
# REGENERATING THIS DEFEATS ITS PURPOSE. A red digest test means the serialized
# bytes MOVED — find out WHY (the C++ side reads these bytes); do NOT regenerate
# to make it pass. See tests/test_plan_bytes.rs for the full rationale.
# Plans are built via the FIXED symlink /tmp/peacock-plan-bytes-root, so the
# absolute parquet paths the wire format embeds are identical on every machine
# and these digests are portable. Path VALUES are therefore held constant, not
# normalized out; the round-trip oracle covers them. Regenerated at c4ddca8 —
# equal to the 9cc44c9 capture by the 131/131 0-drifted proof across Inc3.
